# sha256 lock for open-lakehouse pinned JARs (docs/testing.md — supply chain).
#
# Format: "<sha256>  <filename>" (sha256sum / `shasum -a 256` output).
# download-jars.sh verifies every jar against this on download and in
# --verify-only; a MISMATCH is always fatal.
#
# This lock is UNPOPULATED until generated on a networked machine:
#     ./scripts/tools/download-jars.sh --lock
# then commit the diff. Until then, checksum verification WARNS (non-fatal) and
# only the size check gates. Once populated, flip enforcement on by adding
# --require-checksums to the T0 gate (see docs/testing.md).
